        rules: {
          objective: "Score points by fulfilling a bid contract. Scores are calculated in 'fiches' or chips.",
          gameplay: "1. Standard trick-taking. Must follow suit. If unable, play any card or trump.\n2. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest card of led suit wins.\n3. **Pass**: If everyone passes, a 'General Point-less' hand (Vuile) is played where the goal is simply to win as many tricks as possible, or a redeal occurs.",
          keyRules: [
            'Bidding hierarchy: Prop/Mee, Troel, Abondance, MisÃ¨re, Solo, Piccolo, Grote MisÃ¨re',
            'Must follow suit',
            'Partnerships form during bidding',
            'Troel: automatic partnership if player has 3+ Aces',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'In MisÃ¨re, lead your lowest cards in suits where you only have one or two cards. Your goal is to exhaust a suit so you can safely discard your high cards later.',
          intermediate: "The 'Prop/Mee' partnership: If you see someone 'propose', and you have two Aces or a King-Queen sequence, accept the partnership ('Mee!'). This is the most consistent way to score.",
          advanced: 'Troel Detection: If the dealer has 3 Aces, they must play a Troel. If you have the 4th Ace, you ARE their partner. Use this knowledge to coordinate from the first trick without needing to bid.',
          tips: [
            "In Abondance (9 tricks), your side suits are more important than your trumps. You must have at least one long suit to 'run' for the extra tricks.",
            'Always count the number of cards remaining in the trump suitâ€”a single missing 10 can ruin a Solo bid.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
